  "index": 5,
  "url": "https://app.programiz.pro/course/css-fundamentals-for-webpage/header-menu?page=4",
  "title": "Styling by Location (Descendant Selector)",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Course: CSS Fundamentals for Your First Webpage"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Styling by Location (Descendant Selector)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A very common situation is this:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "\"I want to style something only when it appears inside a specific section.\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "For example, menu items inside the header shouldn't look like content lists."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<header>\n2  <h1>Learning HTML & CSS</h1>\n3  <nav>\n4    <ul>\n5      <li>Home</li>\n6      <li>Lessons</li>\n7      <li>Resources</li>\n8    </ul>\n9  </nav>\n10</header>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "1header li {\n2  list-style: none;\n3}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This reads almost like English:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "\"Select list items that live inside the header.\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Nothing outside the header is touched. That's the power here — context without complexity."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Being Intentional About Depth (Child Selector)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Sometimes location alone isn't enough."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Imagine adding a nested list later — suddenly your styles apply in places you didn't expect. Developers avoid that by being explicit."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1<header>\n2  <h1>Learning HTML & CSS</h1>\n3  <nav>\n4    <ul>\n5      <li>Home</li>\n6      <li>Lessons</li>\n7      <li>Resources</li>\n8    </ul>\n9  </nav>\n10</header>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1nav > ul {\n2  padding: 0;\n3}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This doesn't mean \"any <ul> in the nav\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It means:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "\"Only the <ul> that sits directly inside <nav>.\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This kind of precision keeps CSS predictable as pages grow. It's not about being strict — it's about staying safe."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
    },
